{"groups":[{"members":["c1","c2","c3"],"primary":"c3","title":"California application screening fee cap and conditions (Civ. Code § 1950.6)","requirement":"A landlord or agent may charge an applicant a screening fee only to cover actual out-of-pocket costs of gathering applicant information plus the reasonable value of time spent, up to a CPI-adjusted cap. No fee may be charged if no unit is or will soon be available. The landlord must either use a first-qualified screening process or refund unselected applicants within 7 days, and must provide an itemized receipt, refund any unused portion, and give the applicant a copy of the credit report within 7 days.","key_value":"$30 per applicant statutory base, CPI-adjustable annually from Jan. 1, 1998 (D026, D017); 2026 adjusted maximum stated as $68.96 (D005); refund within 7 days of selection or 30 days of submission, whichever is first (option B)","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.6","coverage_conditions":"Applies statewide to landlords (owners of residential rental property) and their agents charging applicants, including guarantors or cosignors, for residential rental units.","exemptions":"Does not preempt provisions or regulations governing collection of deposits and fees under federal or state housing assistance programs. Under the first-qualified option (A), no refund is required for an applicant denied after consideration for failing established screening criteria.","conflict_note":"c3 (D026) gave effective_date 2026-01-01, but no other candidate supports that date. The statutory text's CPI adjustment beginning Jan. 1, 1998 shows the section was operative long before 2026, so the date was not adopted. The $30 figure (D026, D017) and the $68.96 figure (D005) do not conflict: $30 is the statutory base and $68.96 is the CPI-adjusted 2026 maximum. c1 (D005) says the landlord must use an applicant-provided reusable screening report, while the statutory text in D026 and D017 says the landlord may accept one under § 1950.1. The statutory text was followed."}],"dropped":[]}
